    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d851-a1">

                <pb facs="0691" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg575"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the honor to answer your representation of today relative to yesterday’s
                    telegram from his excellency Secretary Bryan, and to state that the First Chief
                    directs me to say that he appreciates the reports which were furnished him
                    relative to the critical situation through which the capital is passing.</p>
                <pb facs="0692" n="576" xml:id="pg576"/>
                <p>Mr. Carranza has instructed me to communicate to you that, in order to prevent
                    disturbances in the capital of the Republic which might injure foreign
                    interests, he has given proper orders to his representatives in Mexico City that
                    order in that capital shall be preserved. In this way the peaceful inhabitants
                    of the capital will have guaranties of their lives and interests. I reiterate
                    [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Isidro Fabela</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
